    "replacement": "{bpm: 90} {time: 3/4} {key: G}\n\n// Amazing Grace (John Newton, 1779)\n{label: verse}\nG           G7        C      G\nAmazing grace, how sweet the sound\nG               Em      D\nThat saved a wretch like me\nG            G7       C      G\nI once was lost, but now am found\nG      Em       D       G\nWas blind, but now I see\n\nG             G7          C        G\n'Twas grace that taught my heart to fear\nG           Em        D\nAnd grace my fears relieved\nG             G7         C       G\nHow precious did that grace appear\nG       Em      D        G\nThe hour I first believed\n\n{loop: verse 2}\n\n// Ending\nC      G/B    Am7    D7sus4  G*6\n",
    "start": 0,
    "text_revision": 30,
    "undo": "reset"
   },
   "type": "TextEdited"
  },
  {
   "json": {
    "pages": [
     {
      "blocks": [
       {
        "image": null,
        "kind": "text",
        "notation": null,
        "spans": [],
        "text": "Chord Notepad is a text editor for musicians. Write a song the way a chord sheet looks: chords on their own line, right above the lyrics they go with."
       },
       {
        "image": null,
        "kind": "snippet",
        "notation": "american",
        "spans": [
         {
          "end": 1,
          "kind": "chord",
          "message": "",
          "start": 0
         },
         {
          "end": 12,
          "kind": "chord",
          "message": "",
          "start": 9
         },
         {
          "end": 19,
          "kind": "chord",
          "message": "",
          "start": 18
         },
         {
          "end": 26,
          "kind": "chord",
          "message": "",
          "start": 25
         },
         {
          "end": 60,
          "kind": "chord",
          "message": "",
          "start": 58
         },
         {
          "end": 66,
          "kind": "chord",
          "message": "",
          "start": 64
         },
         {
          "end": 72,
          "kind": "chord",
          "message": "",
          "start": 71
         },
         {
          "end": 81,
          "kind": "chord",
          "message": "",
          "start": 80
         }
        ],
        "text": "C        C/E      F      C\nTwinkle, twinkle, little star,\nDm    Am     G        C\nHow I wonder what you are!"
       },
       {
        "image": null,
        "kind": "text",
        "notation": null,
        "spans": [],
        "text": "The app recognizes chord lines on its own and highlights their chords; lyric lines are left alone. In the Play tab, tap any chord to hear it, or press ▶ at the bottom to play the whole song."
       }
      ],
      "title": "Welcome to Chord Notepad"
     },
     {
      "blocks": [
       {
        "image": null,
        "kind": "text",
        "notation": null,
        "spans": [],
        "text": "There is nothing to mark up. A line counts as a chord line when most of its words are chords, so a lyric that happens to contain a word like “A” stays plain text."
       },
       {
        "image": null,
        "kind": "snippet",
        "notation": "american",
        "spans": [
         {
          "end": 1,
          "kind": "chord",
          "message": "",
