          "kind": "chord",
          "message": "",
          "start": 110
         }
        ],
        "text": "G              D/F#        Em          C\nA song for you, a melody I made\nAm7   Dsus4   Cmaj7   G/B   F#m7b5   E7#9"
       },
       {
        "image": null,
        "kind": "text",
        "notation": null,
        "spans": [],
        "text": "Chords can be as rich as you need: sevenths, suspended and added notes, extensions, altered notes, and slash chords for a specific bass note."
       }
      ],
      "title": "How Chord Lines Are Detected"
     },
     {
      "blocks": [
       {
        "image": null,
        "kind": "text",
        "notation": null,
        "spans": [],
        "text": "Prefer solfège? Switch to European notation with the Do button in the Edit ribbon and write chords as Do, Re, Mi… with a lowercase m for minor. Convert rewrites a whole song from one notation to the other."
       },
       {
        "image": null,
        "kind": "snippet",
        "notation": "european",
        "spans": [
         {
          "end": 2,
          "kind": "chord",
