        "text": "{label: chorus}\nF         C         G         Am\nSing it loud and sing it clear,\nF         C         G\neverybody gather near\n// Chorus twice at the end\n{loop: chorus 2}"
       },
       {
        "image": null,
        "kind": "text",
        "notation": null,
        "spans": [],
        "text": "In the Edit tab, ＋ Insert has small dialogs for adding labels, loops and other directives if you'd rather not type them."
       }
      ],
      "title": "Song Structure"
     },
     {
      "blocks": [
       {
        "image": null,
        "kind": "text",
        "notation": null,
        "spans": [],
        "text": "In the Play tab, the panel under the song draws its chords: as a piano roll, on a music staff, as guitar chord diagrams (Fret cards), or as tab. It follows along while the song plays."
       },
       {
        "image": null,
        "kind": "text",
        "notation": null,
        "spans": [],
        "text": "Fret cards and Tab need a fretted instrument, picked with the Voicing button in the Play tab (for example Guitar). The panel shows in the Play tab only; the ▭ button there shows or hides it."
       }
      ],
      "title": "The Chord Sheet"
     },
     {
      "blocks": [
       {
        "image": null,
        "kind": "text",
        "notation": null,
        "spans": [],
        "text": "That's all you need to get started."
       },
       {
        "image": null,
        "kind": "text",
        "notation": null,
        "spans": [],
        "text": "The full User Guide is in ☰ → User guide. Identify in the Edit ribbon names a chord from the notes you pick, and ☰ → Quick start brings this tour back."
       },
       {
        "image": null,
        "kind": "text",
        "notation": null,
        "spans": [],
        "text": "Have fun making music!"
       }
      ],
      "title": "You're Ready!"
     }
